What this license covers, and what it does not

The MIT License above covers the code of this project: the Python package, the
page templates, the stylesheet, the schemas, the tests and the documentation.

It does not cover a parish's data. The readings a parish enters in its own copy
(the files under data/) and the figures its site publishes from them (the pages
and the feed under /api/v1/) belong to that parish. Each parish shares its
published data under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license
(CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), as its feed's
index.json states. The sample data shipped with the template is fictional and
may be used freely.

The emission factors in data/factors.csv are published by the United States
Environmental Protection Agency; each row records its source.

The Noto fonts in static/fonts/ are licensed separately under the SIL Open Font
License, Version 1.1 (static/fonts/OFL.txt).
